# What the ITM edition leaves out, ON TOP of system/release/public-export.gitignore.
#
# The public filter keeps out what is personal. This list keeps out what is
# fine to publish but is not part of the core a colleague should meet on day
# one: specialists for one platform or for building Metis itself, the course
# machinery, background packs, and the development tooling.
#
# Same syntax as .gitignore, matched against `git ls-files` of the development
# repository by editions/export-edition.sh.

# ── Editions are built from here; the copy never carries the build itself ──
editions/

# ── Specialists outside the core roster ─────────────────────────────────────
# Kept: metis, librarian, writing-partner, methods-coach, biostatistician,
# epidemiologist, data-analyst, data-guardian, meeting-memory, news-radar,
# presentation-maker, visualization-maker, critic, memory-curator, phd-architect,
# research-architect, career-coach, software-engineer, content-harvester,
# cybersecurity (the pipeline's own safety checks call it).
agents/dhis2-expert/
agents/dashboard-engineer/
agents/course-builder/
agents/learning-coach/
agents/learning-architect/
agents/edu-expert/
agents/rc-builder/
agents/builder/
agents/hr-talent/
agents/background-maker/
agents/news-aggregator/
agents/frontend-designer-builder/
agents/design-auditor/
agents/ux-engineer/
agents/hat-*
